<doc id="80861" url="https://jv.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=80861" title="Muhammad Arsyad al-Banjari">
Muhammad Arsyad al-Banjari

Syekh Muhammad Arsyad bin Abdullah bin Abdur Rahman al-Banjari (utawi langkung misuwur kanthi asma Syekh Muhammad Arsyad al-Banjari (#ALIH utawi 15 Shofar 1122 – 6 Syawwal 1227 H) inggih punika ulama &lt;a href="fiqih"&gt;fiqih&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href="madahab%20Syafi%27i"&gt;madahab Syafi'i&lt;/a&gt; ingkang asalipun saking Kutha &lt;a href="Martapura"&gt;Martapura&lt;/a&gt; ing &lt;a href="Tanah%20Banjar"&gt;Tanah Banjar&lt;/a&gt; (&lt;a href="Kasultanan%20Banjar"&gt;Kasultanan Banjar&lt;/a&gt;), &lt;a href="Kalimantan%20Kidul"&gt;Kalimantan Kidul&lt;/a&gt;. Panjenenganipun gesang watawis taun 1122-1227 hijriyah. Panjenenganipun pikantuk gelar Datu Kelampaian. Panjenenganipun punika dados panyerat Kitab Sabilal Muhtadin ingkang dados rujukan tumrap tiyang &lt;a href="Islam"&gt;Islam&lt;/a&gt; ing wewengkon &lt;a href="Asia%20Kidul-W%C3%A9tan"&gt;Asia Kidul-Wétan&lt;/a&gt;. Muhammad Arsyad Al-Banjari, ingkang ugi dipuntimbali Tuanta Salamakka lan Datuk Kalampayan. Panjenenganipun punika putra kapisan saking gangsal sadhèrèk, ramanipun namanipun ‘Abd Allah lan ibunipun namanipun Siti Aminah. Muhammad Arsyad miyos saking kulawarga ingkang kawentar tangat agaminipun. Kondhisi lingkungan ingkang saé punika saged damel kapribadénipun Muhammad Arsyad ing wekdal salajengipun.
<h2>Trah</h2>
Trah.
Wonten sawatawis panyerat biografi gadhah pamanggih bilih panjenenganipun punika taksih trah &lt;a href="Alawiyyin"&gt;Alawiyyin&lt;/a&gt; kanthi jalur Sultan Abdurrasyid Mindanao. Nasab utawi trah Syekh Muhammad Arsyad bin Abdullah bin Abdur Rahman al-Banjari inggih punika: Maulana Muhammad Arsyad Al Banjari bin Abdullah bin Abu Bakar bin Sultan Abdurrasyid Mindanao bin Abdullah bin Abu Bakar Al Hindi bin Ahmad Ash Shalaibiyyah bin Husein bin Abdullah bin Syaikh bin Abdullah Al Idrus Al Akbar (datuk sadaya kulawarga Al Aidrus) bin Abu Bakar As Sakran bin Abdurrahman As Saqaf bin Muhammad Maula Dawilah bin Ali Maula Ad Dark bin Alwi Al Ghoyyur bin &lt;a href="Muhammad%20al-Faqih%20Muqaddam"&gt;Muhammad Al Faqih Muqaddam&lt;/a&gt; bin Ali Faqih Nuruddin bin &lt;a href="Muhammad%20Shahib%20Mirbath"&gt;Muhammad Shahib Mirbath&lt;/a&gt; bin Ali Khaliqul Qassam bin Alwi bin Muhammad Maula Shama’ah bin Alawi Abi Sadah bin Ubaidillah bin Imam &lt;a href="Ahmad%20al-Muhajir"&gt;Ahmad Al Muhajir&lt;/a&gt; bin Imam Isa Ar Rumi bin Al Imam Muhammad An Naqib bin Al Imam &lt;a href="Ali%20al-Uraidhi"&gt;Ali Uraidhy&lt;/a&gt; bin Al Imam &lt;a href="Ja%27far%20ash-Shadiq"&gt;Ja’far As Shadiq&lt;/a&gt; bin Al Imam &lt;a href="Muhammad%20al-Baqir"&gt;Muhammad Al Baqir&lt;/a&gt; bin Al Imam &lt;a href="Ali%20bin%20Husain"&gt;Ali Zainal Abidin&lt;/a&gt; bin Al Imam Sayyidina &lt;a href="Husain%20bin%20Ali"&gt;Husein&lt;/a&gt; bin Al Imam Amirul Mu’minin &lt;a href="Ali%20bin%20Abi%20Thalib"&gt;Ali bin Abi Thalib&lt;/a&gt; Karamallah wajhah wa Sayyidah &lt;a href="Fatimah%20az-Zahra"&gt;Fatimah Az Zahra&lt;/a&gt; binti &lt;a href="Muhammad"&gt;Rasulullah SAW&lt;/a&gt;.
